{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirl-unc/hitlist/pulls/846","id":5003695813,"node_id":"PR_kwDOR0xlYM8AAAABKj5WxQ","html_url":"https://github.com/pirl-unc/hitlist/pull/846","diff_url":"https://github.com/pirl-unc/hitlist/pull/846.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pirl-unc/hitlist/pull/846.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirl-unc/hitlist/issues/846","number":846,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Preserve nominal-dose MS evidence and source lineage for PXD024809","user":{"login":"iskandr","id":48441,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NDQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48441?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr","html_url":"https://github.com/iskandr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iskandr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"PXD024809 provides nominal-dose standards in a serially diluted JY HLA-eluate matrix. Its aligned quantities, scored candidates and transition library use distinct identifiers and missingness states; treating aligned quantities alone as detected concentrations loses essential evidence.\n\nAdd `write_dilution_observer_package`, `verify_dilution_observer_package` and 15 relations through the existing `EvidenceStore`. The revision pins 17 originals and preserves all literal cells, large IDs, exact form/charge/target library membership, feature links/comparisons, the full standard panel, nominal levels and scoped protocol/material claims. Independent source snapshots and typed recompilation reject altered evidence after manifest rehash. Version **2.0.40**; current head **1b3ad56**.\n\nDIA1/DIA2 have different reported acquisition windows and are not assumed exchangeable replicates. Missing library standards are not negatives. Nominal solution amounts are not certified on-column amounts; the twofold-versus-1:10 conflict and unknown recovery/actual-parameter claims remain explicit. This is a source package, not an admitted calibration recipe or a model of intracellular abundance.\n\nValidation and pending gates:\n- Format and lint pass. The six catalog test files plus source fixtures pass 48 checks; the later subprocess-catalog correction plus source fixtures pass 26 checks (overlapping set).\n- Latest hosted unit jobs pass on Python 3.10–3.14; lint/docs pass. Integration job **121139728815**, workflow **40183613623**, is still running. The earlier single stale-catalog CI failure (3,568 other tests passed) is preserved as a byte-restorable compressed job log.\n- Full local tests remain pending: two unchanged preflights refused before pytest at 0.25/0.08 GiB free plus speculative memory.\n- [Independent original-source audit](https://github.com/pirl-unc/presto/tree/50a2af40f32cad0f297d71884c9215310f17011d/experiments/2026-10-25_0844_codex_dilution-scoring-lineage) verifies 1,031,853 rows / 29,039,248 cells and exact cross-file lineage.\n- [Canonical build/replay preparation](https://github.com/pirl-unc/presto/tree/d92606a4ec2cde5cd9f9edd255a62108203f6556/experiments/2026-10-25_0959_codex_dilution-canonical) freezes this implementation and a separate literal/rational checker. Its 13 software-boundary tests pass. **No original canonical package or independent canonical replay has run:** build attempt 1 refused at 69.88 MiB versus the unchanged 3 GiB startup floor and launched no child.\n- Before readiness: full local suite, canonical materialization and independent source reconciliation, all final hosted gates, review, merge and verified tested PyPI publication. This remains draft.\n\nRefs #845; the later nominal-dose training recipe remains separately gated.\n","created_at":"2026-10-25T09:57:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T10:19:33Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"56655e5096ec73ee5dd9b3fd2a8a5afb5702c121","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirl-unc/hitlist/pulls/846/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirl-unc/hitlist/pulls/846/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirl-unc/hitlist/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirl-unc/hitlist/issues/846/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirl-unc/hitlist/statuses/1b3ad5639a7bbbea7a24fdde41c25e12a1bc2511","head":{"label":"pirl-unc:codex/pxd024809-observation-20261025","ref":"codex/pxd024809-observation-20261025","sha":"1b3ad5639a7bbbea7a24fdde41c25e12a1bc2511","user":{"login":"pirl-unc","id":71463575,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjcxNDYzNTc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71463575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc","html_url":"https://github.com/pirl-unc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirl-unc/received_e